  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="347972f0-6451-5dcd-98d4-bece99baba9c" activityNameId="c654c6d6-7830-524b-994a-71c0ae648970" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Energy reduction, ventilation system, 6 x 120 m3/h, steel ducts, without GHE</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Energy reduction, ventilation system, 6 x 120 m3/h, steel ducts, without GHE
The module reflects the impact of the ventilation system in relation to the benefit. It can be used for comparison with other systems for heat production. The date bases on a operation of the ventilation system of 12 month per year.;
UUID: 87cc8808-b179-3352-bef6-80e223edbdf5
Materials and energy used for ventilation of dwellings in relation to the heat demand reduction for a low energy building.
Location: Data representative for a low energy building in Zurich, Switzerland
Technology: Reduction of 31.2 MJ/(m2 a) heat demand representative for a low energy building in Zurich and a room temperature of 20°C. Heat demand of the building without ventilation system 105 MJ/(m2 a) according to SIA 380/1. Electricity demand of ventilator (0.4 Wh/m3) representative for DC- or EC-motors and a system design with low pressure drops. Electricity demand of control unit 10 W. Additional 0.3 kWh/(m2 a) electricity demand for defrosting of heat exchanger. Electricity mix for Switzerland used. Ventilation system without ground heat exchanger and 6 decentral ventilation units with an air exchange rate of 120 m3/h each. Distribution of fresh- and exhaust-air within the flat with galvanised steel ducts (100x50 mm).
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Calculations, technical information and assumptions. Data valid for example building used. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_87cc8808-b179-3352-bef6-80e223edbdf5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
